        lql: ['LQ and LQ-L', 'The LQ model bends the survival curve ever more steeply, which overestimates the effect of very large fractions. LQ-L (Astrahan 2008) follows LQ up to a transition dose d_T and continues along the tangent above it: BED = d_T(1 + d_T/(α/β)) + (1 + 2d_T/(α/β))(d − d_T). d_T is set as a multiple of each tissue\'s α/β (default 2, so 20 Gy for α/β 10 and 6 Gy for α/β 3). Use it to see how much a result with large fractions depends on the model; it is not validated clinically.'],
        guidance: ['RCR guidance: 2019 or 5th edition draft', 'Both editions keep the same decision order and categories. With the 5th edition draft: (1) 1-week breast schedules get no extra dose for an interruption and should finish within 3 weeks where possible; (2) 3-week breast schedules should not exceed an overall time of 5 weeks; (3) medulloblastoma aims for a total time under 45 days; (4) BID on a chemotherapy day is excluded only when the chemotherapy is not daily or d > 1.5 Gy, while the 2019 text advises against accelerated treatment on any day of concomitant chemotherapy. In both editions SABR resumes on non-consecutive days.'],
